      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding on:\n\n* A world's UI can enable descriptive text for those who have color blindness settings enabled.\n\n* A big world can provide instantanious options for transitions between areas when the user uses Holoport Locomotion.\n\n* A world can hide NPCs if they get too close to the player with Personal Space enabled.\n\nThese things I feel can be used in ways to maliciously target those with accessibility settings enabled. So an option to have the user selectively hide options from the world like as currently would help. Hiding would give default values to the world and the world would be unaware if the player hid their settings.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-25T23:25:13.804Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It would be useful to have a way to only get generic user settings like when Comfort Turning is enabled or what FOV a desktop player is using. This would allow us to adapt world experiences based on their own personal settings on VRC without having to ask them in world.\n\nFor example: \n\n* A custom character controller can automatically use the Comfort Turning setting for snapping to increments or smooth turning.\n\n* A horror world can reduce it's intensity from the player's chosen Content Filter settings (tho normally the world would be hidden from the user if it did mark itself properly).\n\n* A in world object can adjust it's size to accommodate for an increased FOV.\n\n* A theater world can put a warning stating that the user has Avatar Culling enabled and recommends the user to disable it for the best experience.\n\n* A world can provide assistance, prompt user volume adjustments, and/or give a bigger indicator to other players if the player has earmuffs enabled.\n\nThere is a `GetBoolInputSetting` & `SetBoolInputSetting` function from the InputManager, however, it seems to be specific for VRChat's worlds.\n\nSome of these settings are detectable via extreme work arounds or via asking the player directly but some are unable to be checked for like Personal Space.",
